<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Custoza (1866)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-italian-war-of-independence">Third Italian War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Custoza was fought on 24 June 1866 near Verona during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-italian-war-of-independence">Third Italian War of Independence</a>, part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-prussian-war">Austro-Prussian War</a>. An Austrian army under Archduke Albrecht defeated a larger but poorly led Italian army under Alfonso La Marmora. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> nonetheless gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a> at the peace, because <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> won the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-custoza-1866.jpg" alt="Battle of Custoza (1866)" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juliusz Kossak · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Custozza1866.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Italy’s armed forces were built on the Piedmontese army, but early campaigns were disappointing: in 1866 Italy lost to Austria on land at <b>Custoza</b> and at sea at Lissa, gaining Venetia only because Prussia won the war.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy · Military</a></li></ul></section>
